---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q4 = `A hiring program scores applicants. One of the
variables it uses is the applicant's salary at
their previous job.

The program contains no errors. Its arithmetic is
correct. It produces the same score for the same
inputs every time.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 22</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Nine questions &middot; 15 minutes &middot; Impact of Computing
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>
            <b>Topics 5.1 to 5.5 &mdash; activities 3.11 to 3.15.</b> Beneficial and
            harmful effects, the digital divide, computing bias, crowdsourcing, and
            legal and ethical concerns.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>These questions are about precision, not opinion.</b> Every one of them
            has a wrong answer that sounds reasonable, and the difference is usually
            whether an option names <b>who</b> and <b>why</b>.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 15 minutes.</b> Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or{" "}
            <b>unsure</b>. Guess rather than leave a blank.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>
            A navigation app tracks a car's speed and position to predict its arrival
            time. The same data is later used by an insurer to raise the driver's
            premium. Which best describes this situation?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) The app has two separate effects, one beneficial and one harmful</li>
            <li>(B) A single effect of the app is viewed as beneficial by one party and harmful by another</li>
            <li>(C) The app has been misused, so its effects are not the developer's concern</li>
            <li>(D) The harmful effect shows the app was poorly designed</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>Which of these is <b>not</b> a computing innovation?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) E-commerce</li>
            <li>(B) Photo editing software</li>
            <li>(C) A paper road atlas</li>
            <li>(D) A self-driving car</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3</h3>

          <p>
            Which statement about the digital divide is <b>most</b> accurate?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) It describes the gap in internet access between wealthy and poor countries</li>
            <li>(B) It is a consequence of technology advancing faster than people can learn it</li>
            <li>(C) It refers to differing access to computing devices and the internet based on socioeconomic, geographic or demographic characteristics, affecting both groups and individuals</li>
            <li>(D) It refers to the difference in skill between people who program and people who only use software</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <Code code={Q4} frame="code" lang="txt" title="A Hiring Program" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <p>Which statement is best supported?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) The program cannot be biased, because it contains no errors and is consistent</li>
            <li>(B) The program may reflect existing human bias through the data it uses and the variable it was written to use</li>
            <li>(C) The bias could be removed by collecting salary histories for more applicants</li>
            <li>(D) The bias is intentional, because someone chose to include the variable</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5 &mdash; Select all that apply</h3>

          <p>
            Which are supported by the framework as ways bias can enter a computing
            innovation?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Bias written into the algorithm</li>
            <li>(B) Bias present in the data the innovation uses</li>
            <li>(C) Bias embedded at any level of software development</li>
            <li>(D) Bias introduced only by programmers who intend to discriminate</li>
            <li>(E) Bias that can be eliminated by collecting a larger dataset</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 6</h3>

          <p>
            Researchers ask members of the public to photograph and log frog sightings in
            their own neighborhoods using their own phones. This is best described as:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) crowdsourcing, but not citizen science, because the contributors are not scientists</li>
            <li>(B) neither, because the data will not be reliable enough to publish</li>
            <li>(C) distributed computing, because the work is spread across many devices</li>
            <li>(D) citizen science, which is research conducted in part by distributed individuals using their own computing devices</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 7</h3>

          <p>
            A student downloads an open source library, uses it in their program, and does
            not mention it anywhere. The library's license permits free use and
            modification. Which statement is accurate?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) This is acceptable, because the license permits the use</li>
            <li>(B) This is acceptable only if the student modified the library</li>
            <li>(C) The use is permitted, but material created by someone else should always be cited</li>
            <li>(D) This is not permitted, because open source libraries may not be used in schoolwork</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 8</h3>

          <p>
            Which best describes what <b>Creative Commons</b> is?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) A public copyright license that enables free distribution of an otherwise copyrighted work</li>
            <li>(B) The absence of copyright, placing a work in the public domain</li>
            <li>(C) A category of programs made freely available for redistribution and modification</li>
            <li>(D) Research output published free of restrictions on access</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 9</h3>

          <p>
            A programmer releases a small tool used by twelve people. Two years later it
            is used by four million, and is being used for something the programmer never
            intended. Which statement is best supported?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) The programmer was negligent, since a responsible developer considers every possible use</li>
            <li>(B) Rapid sharing and large numbers of users can produce impacts beyond the programmer's intended purpose or control</li>
            <li>(C) The unintended use is not an effect of the innovation, since it was not designed for it</li>
            <li>(D) Impacts beyond the intended purpose are always harmful</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Nine answers, each marked <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, plus how far you got
            when the timer went off. Worth <b>4 points</b>, graded on completion.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>And one written answer, in two or three sentences:</b> Question 1's option
            (A) says the app has two separate effects. Explain why (B) is the better
            description, using the word <b>feature</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
